  "assessments": [
    {
      "item": "stop semantics and ownership",
      "judgment": "new does not fill; record does not fill; loop try_recv precedes fill, then biased stop before join and loop-top recheck. Stop boundary is observation rather than OS arrival instant. StopSourceClosed and SignalFailed separate from Requested. abort_all followed by full join preserves true already-completed Check/JoinError and only actual is_cancelled yields Cancelled. by_ref consumes pending Input ownership into Unstarted without fake task identity/time. Id registry removed exactly once and into_batch asserts empty tasks/registry before original-index sorting."
    },
    {
      "item": "seven checks and complete source",
      "judgment": "All private helpers/readiness paths supplied, starter limited dead_code allowances explained before use. Seven checks cover zerojobs/empty priority, prequeued noGET, twoheld cancellation with duplicated pending URL, refill keeping HTTP200 at original3 and held1/4 cancelled, synthetic completed Check+panic+cancelled+pending, SignalFailed/closed, and ordinary mixed9hits. finish snapshots task/registry before fallback drain so tests cannot repair missing product wait and pass. Controlled select borrows both owners, stores observed state on owner-side scope, finite15seconds, then abort/drain and shutdown before assertions. Current-thread synthetic capacity2 completion notifications immediately precede return/panic, so true finished-not-joined state is established. Starter one pass/six fail and partial record+drain two pass/five fail align with source."
    },
    {
      "item": "signal demo",
      "judgment": "Signal select polls ctrl_c first before sending entered, early event closes entered but carries real reason through same stop channel. finish_controller aborts+awaits and distinguishes task panic. Demo owns Scheduler, Fixture, handle across finite entered/run/ready observations; close awaits scheduler, then saves both listener and server completion before propagating. Request at READY gives input1/3 Cancelled and4/5 Unstarted,2hits,130 after print+flush. Without signal both first requests time out at10seconds; repeated held0 has no remaining gate and returns503, invalid input stays a problem, so ordinary finish1 precedes15second observation. Error and output failure2. OS SIGINT listener permanence/caller drop warning accurate."
    },
    {
      "item": "closure and SVG",
      "judgment": "Four input/single copies equal own sealed B3 sources; all seven Fixture/http-single normal dependencies unchanged from own previous seal; tests equal complete cfg(test) suffix. No dependency examples/binary/integration/cfgtest loaded by selected B4 commands. Complete manifests/core/tests/demo all inline. 27 snippet anchors resolve. SVG source uses gate0/1 separately from original1/4 and depicts final original1/3/4/5/6 classification faithfully."
    }
